From: minpeter <62207008+minpeter@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: drm/h713: Add Allwinner H713 display driver

Add a DRM/KMS driver for the display engine of the Allwinner H713
projector SoC (developed on the HY320 board, 1920x1080 LVDS panel):

- one CRTC that adopts the panel mode the boot loader set up;
- a primary plane (XRGB8888) on the RGB channel and an overlay plane
  (NV12/NV16, 1:1 or scaled 1280x720 -> 1920x1080) on the video
  channel, with global alpha; the RGB raster is lined up with the video
  raster when both planes are shown;
- vblank from the RGB channel's frame-done interrupt; flip events once
  the hardware has taken the new address;
- picture controls as CRTC properties (saturation, hue, white balance,
  contrast, brightness, sharpness, dither class) and GAMMA_LUT, written
  in the vblank interrupt and read back.
- the HDMI input (1080p60) as the video plane's source: receiver
  bring-up, lock detection, capture into a ring in reserved memory and
  slot rotation at the video vsync; selected with the CRTC property
  video_source, with read-only status properties. EDID and hot-plug
  come from the board's ARISC driver where its header exists.
- with V4L2 in the kernel, the same HDMI input as a V4L2 capture device
  ("h713-hdmirx-clean"): DV timings (1080p60), source-change events,
  EDID through the ARISC driver, and streaming of the three capture-ring
  slots (NV16M, MMAP, dma-buf export).

The module is a C object (the DRM side) and one Rust object (the
hardware layer: every register access, the register sequences and the
parsers of the board vendor's display data files, which are read
through the firmware loader at run time). The Rust object is a crate
root without module!(); it includes its no_std submodules from shared/.

The driver was written in a clean room from measured register
documents only; the SoC's display co-processor is not used.

Taken from the clean repository's series (cleanroom-h713 drivers/h713-drm/patches/, git format-patch
against v6.18, source state 5fd6cd6), applied to the 7.3.1 tree of this series and regenerated from it.
On 7.3 drivers/gpu/drm/Kconfig lists its sources without blank lines; the source line sits behind sun4i's as in
the v6.18 patch. Nothing else differs from it.

